# Agent layer

Sage is a tool-using helper, not a chatbot with a game-themed prompt.

- Every tool implements `App\Game\Tools\GameTool` and is registered in `AppServiceProvider`.
- `description()` is written for a model: when to call it, what it returns.
- Validate arguments inside `handle()`, even when the caller is trusted.
- Return structured arrays. Failures return an `error` key, not an exception, unless the
  situation is a programming error.
- Tools are read-only until a write path has explicit intent and confirmation (later: a
  confirmation token from the player).
- Never compute values the database owns. Query them.
- Keep the loop bounded (`config/agent.max_steps`) and log tool calls with arguments.
- When the LLM is unavailable, the deterministic path must still call real tools and never
  fabricate data.
- Add or update an eval in `tests/Eval` for any behavior change.
